SUMMARY:Town of York Historical Society - Simcoe Day in Toronto 2026
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Simcoe Day 2026 with Toronto history authors\, booksellers\, podcasters\, and historical societies on Monday\, August 3\, 2026! \nFor a third straight year\, the York Pioneer & Historical Society (YPHS)\, Toronto’s First Post Office (TYHS)\, and the Riverdale Historical Society are partnering to bring together people who share a passion for Toronto’s rich past. \nJoin us from 1:00 p.m. to 4:00 p.m. at St. Matthew’s Clubhouse\, 450 Broadview Avenue (just north of Gerrard Street East) for an afternoon dedicated to exploring Toronto history! \nBrowse curated artifact displays\, meet and chat with local authors and podcasters\, connect with historical societies\, and take part in guided neighbourhood walks. Whether you’re a lifelong history enthusiast or simply curious about Toronto’s past\, you’ll discover something new and meet others who share your interest! \nAdmission is free. \nPlease Note: Some book purchases will be cash only.
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/town-of-york-historical-society-simcoe-day-in-toronto-2026/
LOCATION:St. Matthew’s Clubhouse\, 450 Broadview Ave.\, Toronto\, ON\, M4K 2N1\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN="Town of York Historical Society":MAILTO:info@tos1stpo.com
GEO:43.6682525;-79.3531563
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=St. Matthew’s Clubhouse 450 Broadview Ave. Toronto ON M4K 2N1 Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=450 Broadview Ave.:geo:-79.3531563,43.6682525
END:VEVENT
