SUMMARY:Free Virtual History Lectures with the Diefenbunker: Canada's Cold War Museum
DESCRIPTION:We invite you to join virtually us this fall for the Diefenbunker Museum’s 5th annual Cold War Speaker Series! In this series of free events\, you will hear from experts sharing insights into Canada’s Cold War history. \nAll lectures are free to attend\, and open to all! Advance registration is required to receive the Zoom link and the recording after the event. \nThursday\, August 13\, at 7:00 p.m. ET  \nLove in a Dangerous Time: Canada’s LGBT Purge  \nTo mark Pride Month in the National Capital Region\, hear from the Curator at the Canadian Museum for Human Rights about their exhibition Love in a Dangerous Time: Canada’s LGBT Purge\, followed by a panel discussion with Rainbow Veterans of Canada and LGBT Purge Survivors.
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/free-virtual-history-lectures-with-the-diefenbunker-canadas-cold-war-museum/
LOCATION:online
GEO:56.130366;-106.346771
END:VEVENT
