SUMMARY:Town of York Historical Society - War & Terror in the Town: Annual Summer Walking Tour
DESCRIPTION:Explore the Town of York on foot with our Museum Coordinator! \nIn this walking tour\, join us as we explore the beginnings of the area that would become the Town of York\, the events leading up to the War of 1812\, the Battle of York\, its aftermath\, and everyday living conditions while we walk the original 10 blocks of the early city. \nThis tour begins on the steps of St. James Cathedral (facing King Street East) and end at Toronto’s First Post Office Museum (260 Adelaide Street East). Tours run rain or shine\, and may cover rough ground\, so please dress accordingly. \n–Please Note– \nInformation\, histories\, and stories included our Annual Summer Walking Tours may overlap.
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/town-of-york-historical-society-annual-summer-walking-tour-2026/
LOCATION:Cathedral of St. James\, 106 King Street East\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5C 2E9\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN="Town of York Historical Society":MAILTO:info@tos1stpo.com
GEO:43.6503286;-79.3737598
