SUMMARY:Culinary Historians of Canada: Plenty More - After the War (August webinar)
DESCRIPTION:Scarcity remains in the memory of those who lived during the World War II era. Sugar was a staple that was rationed by government proclamation from 1942 to 1947. It was a key ingredient in preserves\, baked items\, and favourite family dishes. Advertising of sugar during this period used messaging that reflected the societal values derived from the war effort and optimism for better times ahead. \nHistorian Brandi Adams will join us over Zoom for a webinar taking us back to the World War II era and exploring the parallels between mandated food rationing and messaging in sugar advertising. \nTickets available through Eventbrite\nCHC members & students   $15.00\nCulinary Tourism Alliance members   $20.00\nGeneral admission   $23.50\n(Service fees extra) \nA recording will be available for registrants only. No refunds.
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/culinary-historians-of-canada-hearth-baking-eat-make-share-a-taste-of-immigration-2/
LOCATION:online
ORGANIZER;CN="Culinary Historians of Canada":MAILTO:info@culinaryhistorians.ca
GEO:56.130366;-106.346771
END:VEVENT
